WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:06.970
Hey youtubers it’s charlie, this is going
to be my first Last Airbender video.

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:11.210
So many of you requested videos for the original
series that I thought it would be a fun way

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.360
to be less depressed after the Korra finale.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.119
Originally I was going to start by doing a
video for the first episode but I thought

00:00:18.119 --> 00:00:32.940
doing a prologue and an examination of the
unaired pilot would be 

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:37.220
a better way to start.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.650
Even if you know all the episodes by heart,
think of this as a chance to focus on specific

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.019
things in each episode.

00:00:43.019 --> 00:00:47.739
Sometimes you miss a lot of things when you
try to remember details and you haven’t

00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:52.190
watched a show in a long time.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:55.530
It’s like re-watching The Wire on HBO right
now.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.420
Or even the classic simpsons episodes.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.860
I haven’t completely figured out what the
schedule for these avatar videos will be but

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.300
be sure to subscribe to get everything and
dig your episode links out of your bookmarks.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.300
Just for fun I’ll say careful for spoilers.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.760
Maybe some of you haven’t seen last airbender
before.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:07.760
Welcome to the fandom!

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.870
Bryan and Mike pitched Avatar The Last Airbender
to an acquaintance at Nickelodeon in that

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:15.810
period right after Fellowship of the Ring
and the first Harry Potter had come out.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:18.890
The pitch for what would become Last Airbender
was made in 2001.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:20.840
The series didn’t debut till 2005.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:25.620
Just to give you an idea for how long it took
to get through the production process.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:30.760
The two of them weren’t officially known
as Bryke before working on Last Airbender.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.720
They went to college together at the Rhode
Island School of Design.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:34.770
That’s where they met.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:38.110
And they did work on most of the same shows
like Family Guy when it first started, King

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:39.110
of The Hill, Mission Hill and Invader Zim
were the last things they did before Avatar.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:40.540
But they usually worked in different departments
on each of those shows.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:43.200
Bryan spent most of his time working on storyboards
and character design.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.970
And Michael usually worked as an animation
director.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.060
There were both storyboard artists on King
of The Hill though.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.060
They talk a little about it here in this clip.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:52.310
Bryan said that he hated working on King of
the Hill so much he almost quit Hollywood

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:54.240
animation and went to Pixar.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.090
The funny thing is that they said the original
show they were going to pitch to Nick was

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:58.090
completely different from Avatar.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:01.130
Bryan said it was something you would expect
to see on Nickelodeon.

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:04.330
Something that looked and felt like it came
from them, but worked more with spongebob

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:05.330
type programming.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:07.020
He’s never explained what that show was
supposed to be because they still might pitch

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.020
it at some point.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:20.230
So that actually might end up being the next
tv show they produce, even if it’s with

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:39.390
another network like dreamworks animation.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:03:11.090
Most of 

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:33.420
what 

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:44.970
they talk about when they talk about creating
avatar is 

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:47.780
the original proof of concept.

00:03:47.780 --> 00:04:12.739
Bryan’s original sketch for Aang and Appa
and the overseas Korean Animators.

00:04:12.739 --> 00:04:18.560
Bryan is the one who spends most of his time
working with them.

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:24.580
The original overseas animation director on
Avatar, Jae-Myung Yu, this guy right here

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:28.050
was able to create Studio Miir specifically
for Legend of Korra.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:32.300
When it came time to make Legend Of Korra,
because Nick had ordered all the book 1 episodes

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:35.770
up front, Team Bryke had the money to hire
an animation studio.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:38.669
They wanted Yu to do the series, but he was
working somewhere else.

00:04:38.669 --> 00:04:44.319
So he left to create Studio Miir and they
did the episodes.

00:04:44.319 --> 00:04:47.900
Since then they’ve grown as a korean animation
studio and worked on other series.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:51.449
And they have a big deal they just signed
with Dreamworks animation for new shows they’re

00:04:51.449 --> 00:04:54.310
working on but they’re not avatar shows.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:05:03.229
But just to be clear, Studio Miir and Team
Bryke are two separate entities, they don’t

00:05:03.229 --> 00:05:06.620
have any ownership in Studio Miir.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:10.819
DR Studio were the animators on Last Airbender.

00:05:10.819 --> 00:05:15.470
They mostly do anime productions but they’ve
also done a lot of hollywood stuff like some

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:27.860
of the DC and Marvel animated movies and other
Nickelodeon stuff.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:33.029
Jeremy Zuckerman and Bejamin Wynn did all
the music, as they did for Legend of Korra.

00:05:33.029 --> 00:05:38.889
But just like with Studio Miir, because of
the work they did on the Original Avatar Series,

00:05:38.889 --> 00:05:42.669
they were able to create their own production
company called The Track Team.

00:05:42.669 --> 00:05:46.119
They score other hollywood stuff, but it’s
cool to know that Avatar was able to give

00:05:46.119 --> 00:05:47.830
rise to all these new studios.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:50.150
Sometimes that will happen on bigger shows
and movies.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:57.319
A few people land a deal for a new show, and
build a team around them to make it.

00:05:57.319 --> 00:06:02.550
And each of the departments build teams around
them.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:08.050
The very first episode they ever produced
was the unaired pilot.

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:13.669
They changed a lot of the story before they
aired the first official episode on February

00:06:13.669 --> 00:06:14.669
1st, 2005.

00:06:14.669 --> 00:06:18.539
The pilot was only about 15 minutes long,
here’s a breakdown of the stuff they ended

00:06:18.539 --> 00:06:19.539
up changing:

00:06:19.539 --> 00:06:24.200
The four images shown in the opening sequence
of Aang bending do not follow the order of

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.200
the Avatar Cycle.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:31.870
Instead, they go from air, to water, followed
by fire, and ending with earth.

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:41.430
There are several bending techniques used
that were not seen in the polished show, such

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:45.120
as the group-fireball created by Zuko and
several of his soldiers.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:52.409
The concept of the Avatar State functioning
as a defense mechanism was similar to its

00:06:52.409 --> 00:06:58.889
concept in the main series, though in the
pilot, Aang would purposely put himself in

00:06:58.889 --> 00:06:59.889
danger to enter it.

00:06:59.889 --> 00:07:04.360
The creators later felt that the concept of
the Avatar State needed to be more complex,

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:16.020
and so, in the series, they initially gave
Aang no control over it, requiring him to

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:21.860
be in genuine danger before he would enter
the state.

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:35.740
Many aspects of the original pilot were later
incorporated into the actual series but in

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:39.409
different fashions:
The serpent that attacked Team Avatar, and

00:07:39.409 --> 00:07:45.379
later Zuko's ship, was recycled in "The Serpent's
Pass" and "The Awakening".

00:07:45.379 --> 00:07:57.810
The Fire Nation soldier armor design 
is significantly different from the original

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:02.869
series' primary design but an earlier Fire
Nation armor seen in "The Southern Air Temple"

00:08:02.869 --> 00:08:15.879
and "The Siege of the North, Part 1" share
similarities to the original design.

00:08:15.879 --> 00:08:19.939
Zuko and Aang's scaffolding battle was re-used
in "Return to Omashu" during Aang's fight

00:08:19.939 --> 00:08:20.939
with Azula.

00:08:20.939 --> 00:08:24.429
Zuko's messenger hawk chasing Momo was recycled
in "The Waterbending Scroll" where the pirate

00:08:24.429 --> 00:08:28.919
captain's iguana parrot chased Momo and in
"The Runaway" where Momo and Hawky do not

00:08:28.919 --> 00:08:29.919
get along.

00:08:29.919 --> 00:08:35.820
Aang saving Zuko at the last minute was recycled
in "The Blue Spirit" and "The Siege of the

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:36.820
North, Part 2".

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:45.990
Sokka saving himself and Kya by tossing his
boomerang attached to a rope to Aang as he

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:49.940
flew over on his glider was re-used in "The
Northern Air Temple" though there Sokka saved

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:50.940
himself and the mechanist.

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:55.120
Although Kya is renamed Katara, her "original"
name is recycled as the names for both her

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:56.120
mother anddaughter.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:09:04.100
As Aang airbends in the opening sequence,
a statue of a lion turtle can be seen.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:11.890
While the early concept of Pakku waterbends
in the opening sequence, the Northern Water

00:09:11.890 --> 00:09:25.980
Tribe in the background looks more like a
castle than how it is depicted in the final

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:28.480
version.

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:42.080
The prototype of Toph seen in the opening
sequence was later recycled as The Boulder,

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:43.720
Sud, and Bolin.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:45.830
Next video - epsiode 1 - schedule - when to
watch.

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:47.150
favorite things to pick out.

00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:49.780
- probably saturdays, doesn’t mean I won’t
do other anime series.

